═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                                  ABOUT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  QUADRATE is a stack-based programming language that compiles to native
  machine code via LLVM. Inspired by Forth, but with modern amenities like
  static typing, modules, structs, and closures.

  THE STACK IS ALL YOU NEED.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                               FEATURES
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  [*] Stack-based execution model
  [*] Compiles to native code via LLVM
  [*] Static type checking
  [*] Module system with standard library
  [*] Structs and arrays
  [*] First-class functions and closures
  [*] Defer statements for cleanup
  [*] Built-in testing framework
  [*] Language server (LSP) for IDE support
  [*] Code formatter and linter

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                             QUICK START
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  1. EXTRACT THE SOURCE

     tar xzf SOURCE.TGZ
     cd quadrate

  2. BUILD

     make release

  3. INSTALL (optional)

     sudo make install

  4. RUN YOUR FIRST PROGRAM

     echo 'fn main() { "Hello, World!" print nl }' > hello.qd
     quad run hello.qd

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                            REQUIREMENTS
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  - C++20 compiler (GCC 10+ or Clang 10+)
  - LLVM 14 or higher
  - Meson build system
  - A POSIX-compatible operating system (Linux, BSD, macOS)

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                              EXAMPLE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  use math

  fn factorial(n:i64 -- result:i64) {
      n 1 <= if { 1 } else { n n 1 - factorial * }
  }

  fn main() {
      "Factorial of 10: " print
      10 factorial print nl

      "Square root of 2: " print
      2.0 math::sqrt print nl
  }

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
                              TOOLCHAIN
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  quad      - Unified CLI (recommended)
  quadc     - Compiler
  quadfmt   - Code formatter
  quadlint  - Static analyzer
  quadlsp   - Language server
  quadpm    - Package manager
  quadrepl  - Interactive REPL
  quaduses  - Import manager

